<h2>Hidden Fire Damage</h2>
<p>Fire damage is rarely limited to the room where it started. Common items that are missed or underestimated include:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Smoke and soot</strong> throughout the home, including inside walls, attics, and the HVAC system. See <a href="/services/smoke-damage-claims/">smoke damage claims</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Heat damage</strong> to wiring, windows, roof decking, and finishes in nearby rooms.</li>
<li><strong>Water damage</strong> from firefighting, which can soak drywall, insulation, and flooring and lead to mold if not dried.</li>
<li><strong>Structural damage</strong> to framing, trusses, and masonry that may require an engineer&rsquo;s evaluation.</li>
<li><strong>Odor</strong> that lingers in porous materials and may require removal rather than cleaning.</li>
</ul>

